.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/manager-iter2-brief-failed-iron-law-7-verbatim-spec-recheck.md:10:tags: [process, orchestration, iron-law-7]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/manager-iter2-brief-failed-iron-law-7-verbatim-spec-recheck.md:12:domain: process
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/manager-iter2-brief-failed-iron-law-7-verbatim-spec-recheck.md:21:The iter2 Preparation leader brief listed 8 H2 sections that contradicted the locked Idea Design A at `ideation/staging/design/item-a-codex-skill-structure.md` lines 15-23. Specifically:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/manager-iter2-brief-failed-iron-law-7-verbatim-spec-recheck.md:31:The manager constructed the iter2 revision brief from memory — recalling "the locked 8 sections" imperfectly — rather than `Read`-ing `item-a-codex-skill-structure.md` lines 15-23 into context before authoring. The mistake originates from the iter1 Codex evaluation itself, which also miscalled `when-to-load` as the correct frontmatter. The manager inherited that incorrect finding and propagated it as a "fix-mandate" in the iter2 brief without cross-verifying against the Ideation contract.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/manager-iter2-brief-failed-iron-law-7-verbatim-spec-recheck.md:39:Companion rule: when a delegation brief includes any verbatim content claim, the brief-construction turn should grep-cite the source line range (e.g., "per `item-a-codex-skill-structure.md:15-23`") and that grep must have run in the current session. A citation that was not freshly verified is not a citation — it is a paraphrase.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-subprocess-writes-to-main-tree.md:2:name: codex-subprocess-writes-to-main-tree
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-subprocess-writes-to-main-tree.md:12:domain: process
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-subprocess-writes-to-main-tree.md:21:During Planning iter1 EVAL and T02 EVAL (execution), **both** the Codex evaluator leg and the Claude evaluator leg wrote their artifact files (`overall.md`, perspective files) to the **main-tree** session path (`<main>/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/.../evaluation/iter1/{claude,codex}/`) rather than the worktree-rooted equivalent.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-subprocess-writes-to-main-tree.md:23:**Planning iter1 (Codex leg):** The Codex evaluator subagent invoked `codex exec` from its claude-code CWD (the main tree). Codex wrote 4 artifact files to the main-tree path. The delegation prompt cited the worktree absolute path but the `<worktreePath>` macro was documentation syntax — Codex read it literally and fell back to its CWD-rooted resolution.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-subprocess-writes-to-main-tree.md:25:**T02 EVAL (both Claude + Codex legs):** The Claude evaluator also wrote to the main tree, not just Codex. Both legs' eval artifacts landed at `<main>/.gobbi/.../execution/task-02/evaluation/iter1/{claude,codex}/`. The manager had to relocate all files into the worktree post-hoc.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-subprocess-writes-to-main-tree.md:35:All evaluator subagents (both Claude and Codex legs) run in their own claude-code process, whose default working directory is the main-tree root — the directory where the gobbi session started. When they write files, they resolve paths relative to their CWD.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-subprocess-writes-to-main-tree.md:37:For the Codex leg specifically: `codex exec` inherits the subprocess CWD from the wrapping claude-code agent. Even when the delegation prompt cites worktree absolute paths, Codex's tool calls may resolve relative to its CWD when constructing parent directories — especially when the prompt uses `<worktreePath>` as a documentation macro (not a shell variable Codex resolves). Codex sees the literal string `<worktreePath>` and falls back to its CWD.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-subprocess-writes-to-main-tree.md:52:For the Codex leg specifically: replace every `<worktreePath>/...` macro in the prompt with the literal resolved absolute path string. Add an explicit `cd <absolute-worktree-path>` before the `codex exec` call in the wrapper subagent's brief.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-subprocess-writes-to-main-tree.md:62:After evaluator returns: check that `ls <worktree-path>/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/<sid>/{loop}/evaluation/iter{n}/{claude,codex}/` shows the expected files. If empty, run `find <main-tree> -name 'overall.md' -newer <recent-timestamp>` to locate the stray files.
