58:**Manager ownership.** Decision authority is centralized in the manager. The manager owns **judgment** (what should be done next, in what order), **scope construction** (who has the right context for the next task), and **verification** (that the delivered result matches what was promised). The user holds final authority on direction. The manager never delegates judgment — only execution.
