+# Consistency Perspective
+
+## Artifact Summary
+What: execution-phase consistency check of the T3 `orchestration/SKILL.md` amendment against the eight anchor criteria. Why: this task's main risk is docs-sync drift across a dense multi-anchor edit. How: run the prompt's grep/sed/wc/ls checks, inspect surrounding context, and run whole-file greps for stale gate/count wording.
+
+Memory reads: evaluation prompt; amended full target; baseline count; plan T3 block; idea sections 6.1-6.7 and 7.3; project mistakes `claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md`, `evaluator-false-pass-without-diffing.md`, `section-order-is-part-of-the-contract-not-just-the-set.md`, `design-literal-retire-instruction-without-replacement.md`, and codex write-path mistakes; `evaluation/SKILL.md`; `execution/evaluation.md`. Prior iter: none.
+
+## Locked Frame (Stage 1)
+Scenario C1: Each anchor A1-A8 satisfies its binary success criterion.
+Checklist: A1 strikethrough exists; A2 correction block near Orchestration Mode; A3 link count >= 4; A4 two Chat inter-loop rows; A5 fourth Chat gate named; A6 state persistence schema present; A7 workflow metadata schema present; A8 mode-dispatch branch present.
+
+Scenario C2: Existing workflow schema language remains additive.
+Checklist: `workflow.{step}` or `workflow.{loop}` entries remain; Chat array is added without replacing Auto/linear descriptions.
+
+Scenario C3 (adversarial): A local stale count survives even though the anchor technically passes.
+Checklist: whole-file grep for old or count-bearing wording around Chat gates; table row count and prose count match.
+
+## Stage 2 Findings
+C1 checks: Mostly yes, with all anchors passing. Evidence: A1 line 247 has `~~Mode controls...~~`; A2 line 66 has `CORRECTION` in Orchestration Mode; A3 counts are `chat-mode.md=6`, `auto-mode.md=4`; A4 lines 243-244 are two distinct Chat inter-loop rows; A5 line 405 names the per-task user review gate; A6 lines 362-363 document `workflow.chat.tasks[]` in State persistence; A7 line 469 documents it in Workflow Metadata; A8 lines 84-87 describe Auto linear vs Chat per-task slice dispatch.
+
+C2 checks: Yes. Lines 362 and 467-468 preserve the existing workflow step/runtime descriptions while lines 363 and 469 add Chat-only arrays.
+
+C3 checks: No. Whole-file grep found stale gate-count prose at line 398.
+
+Finding COD-CONS-001
+Type: design_flaw
+Domain: docs-sync
+Confidence: 100
+Severity: Medium
+Evidence: `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/orchestration/SKILL.md:398` says `Chat Mode pauses at three points:` but the table immediately below has four Chat rows at lines 402-405, including the new task-boundary gate. This contradicts Idea section 6.4, which says to add a fourth Chat-mode gate.
+Disposition: open
+
+## Verdict
+VERDICT: REVISE
