+# Overall Evaluation
+
+## Artifact Summary
+What: overall Codex evaluation of T3, the 8-anchor amendment to `orchestration/SKILL.md`. Why: verify the mode-dispatch redesign is correctly reflected in the workflow governor before downstream tasks rely on it. How: combine the seven perspective passes, anchor checks, whole-file stale-wording grep, baseline comparison, and output-path verification.
+
+Memory reads: evaluation prompt; amended worktree `orchestration/SKILL.md`; baseline `87563f3:.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/orchestration/SKILL.md`; `planning/artifacts/plan.md`; `ideation/artifacts/idea.md`; project rule `rules/stub-redirect-format.md`; relevant project mistakes for docs-sync, process, orchestration, and codex evaluation path discipline; `evaluation/SKILL.md`; `execution/evaluation.md`. Prior iter: none.
+
+## Locked Frame (Stage 1)
+Scenario O1: The eight anchors pass with direct command evidence.
+Checklist: every A1-A8 entry has PASS evidence and line references.
+
+Scenario O2: Cross-perspective contradictions are surfaced.
+Checklist: anchor pass does not hide stale prose, user-facing ambiguity, or process violations.
+
+Scenario O3 (adversarial): A technically passing anchor set is still not shippable because a local contradiction would mislead a future manager.
+Checklist: whole-file grep catches stale counts around newly added gates; severity and disposition are explicit.
+
+## Stage 2 Findings
+O1 checks: Yes. All eight anchor checks pass.
+
+O2 checks: No. Consistency and Usage both found the same stale count defect at line 398.
+
+O3 checks: No. The table has the fourth gate, but the lead-in still says three points, so a future reader has contradictory instructions.
+
+Finding COD-CONS-001
+Type: design_flaw
+Domain: docs-sync
+Confidence: 100
+Severity: Medium
+Evidence: `orchestration/SKILL.md:398` says `Chat Mode pauses at three points:` while lines 402-405 list four Chat gate rows.
+Disposition: open
+
+Finding COD-USAGE-001
+Type: design_flaw
+Domain: docs-sync
+Confidence: 95
+Severity: Medium
+Evidence: The same stale count can cause a manager to treat the task-boundary gate as an appendix rather than the fourth Chat gate required by Idea section 6.4 and Plan T3.
+Disposition: open
+
+## Cross-Perspective Tensions
+The anchor set passes, but the consumer-facing wording does not fully agree with the added table. Project and Structure are satisfied because the scoped edits landed in the right places; Consistency and Usage override with REVISE because the stale count is in the exact section future managers will read while deciding Chat gates.
+
+## Karpathy 4 Failure Modes
+Wrong assumptions: Present. The old assumption that Chat pauses at only three points remained after adding the task-boundary gate.
+
+Overcomplexity: Not present. The amendment is concise and link-heavy rather than duplicating the full mode specs.
+
+Orthogonal edits: Not present. The diff maps to the T3 scope.
+
+Imperative over declarative: Not present. The amendment mostly declares mode shape and schema, with detailed procedure delegated to sub-docs.
+
+## Preserve List
+Preserve the line 66 CORRECTION block and line 247 strikethrough pattern.
+
+Preserve the mode dispatch block at lines 84-89.
+
+Preserve the two Chat rows in Inter-loop transition at lines 243-244.
+
+Preserve the `workflow.chat.tasks[]` schema entries at lines 363 and 469.
+
+Preserve the link-out pattern to `chat-mode.md` and `auto-mode.md`.
+
+## Anchor Coverage
+A1: PASS. Line 247 wraps the original second sentence in `~~...~~`.
+
+A2: PASS. Line 66 has a CORRECTION block directly under `## Orchestration Mode`.
+
+A3: PASS. `chat-mode.md` occurs 6 times and `auto-mode.md` occurs 4 times, combined 10 >= 4.
+
+A4: PASS. Lines 243-244 contain two distinct Chat rows in Inter-loop transition.
+
+A5: PASS with related REVISE finding. Line 405 names the per-task user review gate, but line 398 still says three points.
+
+A6: PASS. Lines 362-363 add `workflow.chat.tasks[]` in State persistence while preserving existing workflow step keys.
+
+A7: PASS. Line 469 adds `workflow.chat.tasks[]` in Workflow Metadata while lines 467-468 preserve existing workflow runtime entries.
+
+A8: PASS. Lines 84-87 describe mode dispatch: Auto linear 6-step, Chat per-task slice loop.
+
+## Verdict
+VERDICT: REVISE
