+# Usage Perspective
+
+## Artifact Summary
+What: execution-phase evaluation of whether a manager or future maintainer can correctly use the amended `orchestration/SKILL.md`. Why: this doc is an operational contract; ambiguous gate counts can lead a manager to skip a user review point in Chat Mode. How: read the consumer-facing sections and verify the new Chat flow is understandable from the text.
+
+Memory reads: evaluation prompt; amended `orchestration/SKILL.md`; plan T3 block; idea sections 3.2, 6.4, 6.5, 6.7, and 7.3; project mistakes on whole-file grep and false PASS without diffing; `evaluation/SKILL.md`; `execution/evaluation.md`. Prior iter: none.
+
+## Locked Frame (Stage 1)
+Scenario U1: A manager can identify the Chat task-boundary options from SKILL.md alone.
+Checklist: per-task user review gate is named; options are Next task / Revise / Wrap up; only Wrap up advances to Step 6.
+
+Scenario U2: A manager can distinguish loop-internal gates from the task-boundary gate.
+Checklist: lead-in prose and table row count agree; if three loop-internal gates plus one boundary gate are intended, the text says that explicitly.
+
+Scenario U3 (adversarial): A hurried manager reads the prose lead-in and misses the fourth row.
+Checklist: no stale count such as "three points" remains immediately before the four-row Chat table.
+
+## Stage 2 Findings
+U1 checks: Yes. Line 405 names the per-task user review gate and gives Next task / Revise / Wrap up behavior. Line 244 says only Wrap up advances to Step 6.
+
+U2 checks: No. Line 398 says `Chat Mode pauses at three points:` and lines 402-405 then list four Chat rows. The text does not clarify "three loop-internal points plus one task-boundary gate."
+
+U3 checks: No. `rg -n "three points|task boundary"` returned line 398 for the stale count and line 405 for the fourth gate.
+
+Finding COD-USAGE-001
+Type: design_flaw
+Domain: docs-sync
+Confidence: 95
+Severity: Medium
+Evidence: `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-28-8eed14fb/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/orchestration/SKILL.md:398` says `Chat Mode pauses at three points:`; the table at lines 402-405 has four Chat gates, including the required task-boundary gate.
+Disposition: open
+
+## Verdict
+VERDICT: REVISE

